// `mod`, `div` and `xor` are operator words. Written as calls, `mod(a, b)`,
// they were a bare "expected an expression, found 'mod'" that did not say what
// the word is (reported by an agent testing the language). The hint names the
// operator form.
fn main() -> Void {
    let r: Int = mod(7, 3);
    fx { println(r); }
    ret;
}
